# Fallback safety net for main.py -- NOT required if main.py is already
# kept alive via tmux/screen/systemd (see README.md "Deployment" section,
# which is the recommended way to run this pipeline day-to-day).
#
# main.py already runs its own infinite work loop internally (60s cadence
# for research/design/send/inbox-poll). This cron entry does NOT re-run one
# pass every 5 minutes -- it runs `scheduler.py --check` every 5 minutes,
# which starts main.py in the background ONLY if it isn't already running
# (PID-file guarded). In other words: a crash-recovery check, not a
# scheduled re-execution.
#
# LIMITATION: main.py started this way has no attached terminal, so the
# optional console commands (transfer / status / pause / resume) are not
# usable against it. The sell/negotiate/close/handover flow is fully
# automated and needs no terminal; attach a separate interactive session
# (tmux/screen, same command) only when you want a manual override.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Adjust the paths below to your actual clone location and venv.
#   2. Run `crontab -e` and paste the (adjusted) line below.
#   3. Check `pipeline/scheduler.log` for main.py's output.

*/5 * * * * cd /home/youruser/website-designers/pipeline && /home/youruser/website-designers/venv/bin/python scheduler.py --check >> /home/youruser/website-designers/pipeline/scheduler.log 2>&1
